 This way, as much of the specification will be translated automatically and the user
 can decide how to translate the rest.

-OpenAPI 2.x and 3.x are supported as input formats to this converter.
+OpenAPI 2.x, 3.0.x, and a best-effort subset of 3.1.x are supported as input formats
+to this converter.
+
+#### OpenAPI 3.1
+
+OpenAPI 3.1 schemas use the same primitive, format, collection, object, string enum,
+reference, and composition mappings described below. Input documents are interpreted
+directly; they are not rewritten as OpenAPI 3.0. The same behavior is available for
+parsed models passed to `OpenApiCompiler`.
+
+A `type` containing one non-null type and `null`, such as `[string, "null"]`, maps
+to that type with `alloy#nullable`. This preserves the distinction between a nullable
+value and an optional member. An enum must also admit `null` for this trait to apply.
+Unconstrained schemas (`{}` or `true`) map to Smithy documents. Arrays with omitted
+or unconstrained `items` use document members. Schema `examples` are retained as
+`alloy#dataExamples`.
+
+The pinned Swagger parser accepts boolean schemas within properties and array items,
+but rejects boolean-valued entries directly under `components.schemas` before
+conversion. That parser limitation also applies here.
+
+Numeric `exclusiveMinimum` and `exclusiveMaximum` are combined with inclusive bounds.
+Integer bounds are rounded to the nearest permitted integer. Smithy cannot express
+exclusive bounds on decimal types exactly, so those conversions report a restriction,
+as they do for OpenAPI 3.0.
+
+This is not a complete JSON Schema 2020-12 implementation. Unsupported constraints
+produce conversion diagnostics instead of being hidden by a primitive type match.
+These include non-null type unions, non-string enums, `const`, `not`, `anyOf`,
+conditional schemas, tuple and containment constraints, dependent and unevaluated
+constraints, and validation siblings of `$ref`. Compositions with sibling constraints
+are also unsupported. `$id`, anchors, and custom vocabulary handling require further
+work. Existing best-effort limitations, including default-value conversion and webhook
+operations, also apply.
+
+Use `--validate-input --validate-output` to fail when parsing or conversion reports
+errors. Without output validation, unsupported schemas continue to produce diagnostic
+placeholder shapes as part of the converter's best-effort output.

 Below are examples of how Smithy Translate converts various OpenAPI constructs into
 Smithy.
